  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this
  lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>Use graphing technology to create a scatter plot and find the best fit line.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>What does the best fit line estimate for the \(y\)-value when \(x\) is 100?</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \(y\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        83
      </entry>
      <entry>
        102
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        87
      </entry>
      <entry>
        115
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        91
      </entry>
      <entry>
        107
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        93
      </entry>
      <entry>
        122
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        97
      </entry>
      <entry>
        125
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        97
      </entry>
      <entry>
        127
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        101
      </entry>
      <entry>
